-- title:
--   Erdős–Lovász local lemma, symmetric form, uniform finite probability space (Theorem 1)
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be a finite nonempty set with the uniform probability $\Pr(A) = |A| / |\Omega|$ on its subsets. Let $A_1, \dots, A_n \subseteq \Omega$ be events, thought of as the *good* events, and let $\Gamma(1), \dots, \Gamma(n) \subseteq \{1, \dots, n\}$ form a dependency graph: for every $i$ and every set $S$ of indices with $i \notin S$ and $S \cap \Gamma(i) = \emptyset$, $\Pr\big(A_i \cap \bigcap_{j \in S} A_j\big) = \Pr(A_i) \Pr\big(\bigcap_{j \in S} A_j\big)$.
--
--   Suppose every $\Gamma(i)$ has at most $d$ elements, $\Pr(A_i) \ge 1 - p$ for every $i$, and $p \cdot e \cdot (d + 1) \le 1$. Then
--   $$\Pr\Big(\bigcap_{i=1}^{n} A_i\Big) \ >\ 0,$$
--   so some outcome lies in every good event.
--
--   This is the symmetric local lemma of Erdős and Lovász, Theorem 1 in Ambainis, Kempe and Sattath, obtained as the classical instance of the abstract lemma `QLLL.Valuation.lll_symmetric`. Other formulations exist on the platform, for example `AppliedComb.ManyFaces.local_lemma_symmetric` and `Combinatorics.finite_symmetric_local_lemma`.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper states the classical lemma for bad events $B_i$ on an arbitrary probability space. Here it is stated for the good events $A_i = B_i^{c}$ under the uniform probability on a finite set, and the dependency hypothesis is independence of $A_i$ from intersections of good events. Under the usual notion of mutual independence (from the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the non-neighbours) this hypothesis is implied, so the usual applications are covered.
-- source:
--   A. Ambainis, J. Kempe, O. Sattath, A Quantum Lovász Local Lemma, J. ACM 59(5):24 (2012), arXiv:0911.1696 (numbering of the arXiv version), Theorem 1 (Erdős and Lovász), restated for good events

import Definitions.Def_QLLL_LocalLemma_Basic
import Definitions.Def_QLLL_Classical_KSAT
import Mathlib
import Std.Sat.CNF

open QLLL
open QLLL.SAT
open Finset Std.Sat
variable (Ω : Type*) [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq Ω] [Nonempty Ω]

theorem QLLL.SAT.classical_lll_symmetric {m : ℕ} {A : Fin m → Finset Ω}
    {Γ : Fin m → Finset (Fin m)} {p : ℝ} {d : ℕ}
    (hΓ : (counting Ω).IsDependencyGraph A Γ) (hd : ∀ i, (Γ i).card ≤ d)
    (hA : ∀ i, 1 - p ≤ counting Ω (A i)) (hp : p * Real.exp 1 * (d + 1) ≤ 1) :
    0 < counting Ω (univ.inf A) := by sorry
